Peter Macpherson (PETERMAC@MTT.CA) wrote:
: I need to setup an LN03a so it prints landscape, 3 lines down the page
: - can someone call me at (902) 487-4209 with the escape escape codes
: PLEASE

	Hi, the following line will sets an LN03 printer into landscape
		mode :

	<esc>[!p<esc>[23? J<esc>[15m<esc>1;66r

	where : !p	is a (soft) reset  ( just in case )
		1;66r	tells the printer to start at line 1 and make
			the page 66 lines.

	If you want to start at line 3 you either change this 3;66  or
	in the file to be printed you have 3 lines empty at the beginning.
	There are more escape sequences in the file  SYS$SYSTEM:SMGTERMS.TXT
	and also there is a way to use the LIBRARY utility to extract info
	from certain system setup files ( I do not remember now, symbiont or
	some other files; someone else from DEC knows I'm sure).
	Well not to upset other people on the system , after you did your
	print the printer have to reset to 'normal' portrait format
	( <esc>[!p will do it ). To avoid editing files and put in this
	escape sequences all the time one could set up a symbol to point
	to a little com file which first send the 'landscape' to the printer
	then prints the file in landscape mode and finally 'prints' the
	reset sequence.		I hope this helps.

				Csaba  Harangozo
					oipjenny@ozemail.com.au



