In article <41uteb$edi@itu1.sun.ac.za>, heinkeln@seagoon.ee.sun.ac.za (Leon Heinkelein) writes:
>
>Hello all
>
>I have a short question pertaining to a CD-ROM drive (RRD42) attached to an
>Infoserver 150. In a nutshell :
>
>Is it possible to access the audio functionality of the CD-ROM drive?
>
	Nope.  The LAD protocol doesn't implement IO$_DIAGNOSE.

	Besides, at least in the RRD42 case, audio data *only* goes to the
audio (headphone & RCA) jacks and cannot be made to "come out" the SCSI
port which is what the InfoServer normally does with data.  The InfoServer
is a distributed device server - it's hard to  distribute the audio signal
through the headphones. ;-)

						--Doug

