In article <DE6IAu.88n@has.nl>,
Peter Klix - Has Computer Systems <klix@has.nl> wrote:
>I'm looking for suggestions or even a solution to recover VMS backup data from 
>a tape with a bad spot (records with parity errors). The problem is how to read 
>the data behind the bad spot.

It'd help if you told us what the media was (9-track, I would imagine,
but who knows?) and the tape drive and controller being used.  Most
9-track drives are quite capable of reading beyond a bad block, but as
I understand it, some of the newer SCSI ones make it damn difficult
to do this.  If your data is on 8mm, DAT, or TK50, the firmware
in your drive may absolutely refuse to read past a bad block.  You'll
have to find a data recovery shop that has a drive with modified
firmware to read past the bad place.

Tim. (shoppa@altair.krl.caltech.edu)



