This note is meant to be a "heads-up" notice to all HSJ-40 users in Canada, and
possibly in other parts of the world.

Apparently, Digital's service organization is *extremely* low on spare HSJ-40
controllers.  It took over 24 hours for them to get one for us; there are only
2 spares in all of Canada.

Additionally, the firmware card in the HSJ-40 is not considered by Digital to
be a part that's stocked by the field service organization.  If it fails,
you're on your own, and this includes controllers that are still under
warranty.  The controller will *not* function without it.  We had one extra one
that was delivered by Digital a month or two back, but it too was dead (we
hadn't tested it).  In 9 months that we've had our 2 HSJ controllers, we've now
experienced THREE firmware card failures.  Rumours have it that this may be a
typical failure rate.  Digital Canada has *NO* replacement firmware cards. 
We're getting one from another customer in another province.  Another 18 hours
to get this part here.  From the time the controller failed until a replacement
will be functioning, the elapsed time will be about 60 hours.  Of this, 7
hours was due to us not being notified of the failure - VAXsim+ is running but
didn't catch it.  Neither did the current set of messages for Polycenter
Console Manager (we'll be updating our own to include at least the message that
this event put out).

If you've got an HSJ-40, I'd suggest the following course of action:
- Ask your field service provider if they have a spare controller in your city,
or have them tell you where the closest one is
- Ask if they have a spare firmware card with your revision on it (apparently
2.0 is still current and 2.5 is imminent).
- Take whatever course of action you deem appropriate with this information.

