My group at Digital is actively working on x86-to-Alpha migration techniques
(including binary translation), and I would like to assure you that binary
translation is a perfectly legal and acceptable means of porting code from
one architecture to another.  We've already released two products to move
VAX/VMS and MIPS/ULTRIX code to Alpha, and these products have been used
by thousands of customers.  In fact, the sales are still increasing.

