>I'm interested in this too, I have a VAX 6340 with VMS5.5-HW with
>DECWindows and no manuals for DECWindows and would like to talk to the
>VAX from a SUN station using X Windows.
>
>Any help would be appreciated.
>
If you have TCP/IP running on the VAX, it is possible to send Decwindows
displays to other Xterminals, after you are already logged into the other
machine (Unix, PC with Xvision etc...).  What I wanted XDM for was to run
Decwindows on an Xterminal WITHOUT having to log into one of the Unix
hosts first.

You can get most of the functionality of Decwindows on a remote Xterminal
by doing the following (as WING@tgv.com has pointed out) without having
XDM running:

1) Get a VAX session going on the Xterminal (I use rlogin from a Unix Xterm)
2) $ set display/create/node=NAME_OF_XTERMINAL/transport=tcpip
3) Now you can launch Decwindows applications, such as $ create/term/detach,
or start the whole login process by:
   $ spawn/nowait/input=nl: run sys$system:decw$startlogin
(may have some font trouble, which can be fixed in your decw$user_defaults:
resource.dat files).

As for XDM, I'm now checking into our Multinet distribution (V3.2)...

John



