writes: 
>
>Vinay Gupta (vinay@parcom.ernet.in) wrote:
>: Has anybody tried to install 6 harddisks (or all 7 scsi devices ) 
>: on 2100 server?
>
>:  When i tried to do so, "show config" display only 4 harddisk at
most
>:  and one CDROM drive.Out of 6 total disk 2 disks are internal disk
and
>:  rest 4 are in a shoe box, that is connected via flat unshielded
cable.
>:  Total external SCSI cable length is around 1.5M.
>
>It seems there is a big difference between 2100 server reck mounted
and 
>desktop, anyway i am talking about 2100 server that is reck mounted
and
>model no is "500MP-R"

Vinay,

    You are correct that there is a difference between the 500MP and
500MP-R.

    Basically, the 500MP supports the internal drives in a couple of
storageworks boxes in the pedestal.  The 500MP-R supports 2 RZ's in the
RM box, and the remainder must reside in a seperate (hopefully)
storageworks box.

    This does work, and is configured this way at the factory.  Not the
best, as there is considerable SCSI bus cable internal in the 500MP-R
box.  And the storageworks box adds another 1M before you cable it.  So
you normally end up with 5MB SCSI instead of Fast.

    I would suspect that you may have an address conflict on your
drives.  Check that all 6 drives are different addresses.

                            Jesse




