In article <41ni5p$16f@walrus.megabaud.fi>, torppa@walrus.megabaud.fi (Jarkko Torppa) writes:
> 1987 Vintage Dilog board that has 50pin(same as scsi) and 10 pin connectors.
> only numbers on the board are 153102 REV A on the trace side.
> On the component side two stickers 57145 G and S/N 703Q0331
> 
> Anybody regocnize what is this ?

  Looks like it's either a QD703 (SCSI disk controller emulating DU) or a
QT703 (SCSI tape controller emulating a TU80). I don't think the QT703 was
ever sold, so it's more likely you have the disk flavor. The 10-pin con-
nector has the same pinout as the DLVJ1 (DLV11-J), so if you have that
cable, you can put it in a system and talk to it.

