In article <4157q0$b7r@news.cloud9.net> cs@cloud9.net (Carl S. Shapiro) writes:


Carl> I am trying to boot this DEC Station 5000/125 I just got my
Carl> hands on.  Unfortunately I have no idea how to boot the machine.
Carl> I have tried the following command (but without any luck): boot
Carl> rz(0,3,0)/vmunix What am I doing wrong?  Is there some sort of a
Carl> hardware related FAQ similar t "The Sun Hardware Reference"?

You're trying to use the DECstation [23]100 style booting commands
which won't get you anywhere.  What you need to do is

	boot 3/rzX/vmunix

Where X is the SCSI id of the boot disk.  You can see what devices you
have on the system with the command 'cnfg 3', thought it might be
'cnfg 5' on the 5k/1xx systems, I'm at home and can't check.  If so,
you also have to change the leading 3 on the boot command to a five as
well.  

