Well, first of all I should note that an MV2000 is a pretty
feeble machine - 0.9 MIPS and limited to using ST506 RD-series
disks (the 159MB RD54 being the biggest.)  But running a news
feed on it is *theoretically* possible - bearing in mind that
getting this thing to handle a FULL news feed in real time 
would be like trying to tow a yacht with a moped.

Anyway, you'd need the ultra-bulky ANU NEWS software package
(see comp.news.software.anu-news.)  You'd also need a TCP/IP
package for it if you don't already have one (the erratic
CMU/IP package - vmsnet.networks.tcp-ip.cmu-tek - being free,
and MultiNet from TGV being in my obviously biased opinion the
best [if outside your budget.])

Good luck,

Aaron

