  Do you have the appropriate PALcode for the system, and the ECU disk?
  (This stuff is generally on either the ECU floppy or the ECU CD-ROM.)

  I've heard of similar hangs with dead VGA modules, and I don't remember
  seeing any support for an `APIAN 2MB EISA Video adapter' -- you'll want
  to see if NT thinks it supports this adapter.  Digital sells the Matrox
  MGAI, the #9 GXE and the Qvision with the DECpc AXP 150 with NT systems.

  The part number for the firmware disks appears to be QA-01YAA-HC.  If
  you're actually running firmware 0.7, you'll want to upgrade it.  (You
  will probably end up going in steps, from 0.7 to 1.2 to the current
  version, and you'll want to follow the ECU directions closely.  NT 3.1
  requires at least 1.0, and 3.5 requires at least 1.5.)

  The Compaq QVision is supported by OpenVMS, UNIX and NT -- NT includes
  support for a few other VGA controllers.  See the systems and options
  catalog at http://www.digital.com for details.

  See if unplugging the main keyboard and switching over to the serial
  line console can get you to the chevrons.

  If you are unable to get the system going and you have the correct
  version of NT available, the current PALcode/ECU loaded, and you have
  an NT-supported SVGA controller in the bus, please contact me via e-mail
  and I will see if I can get you in contact with one of the Digital
  Channels / VAR folks, or with the DECpc AXP 150 product manager, and
  you can explain your situation with Darius to him/her.

