spurlock@ix.netcom.com (Steve Spurlock) wrote:

>I need information for a VT like terminal to be able handle being in a
>harsh magnetic environment that measures about 200 gausse

We have a similar problem with a VAXstation colour display in a fairly
low field environment. Digital engineering put in quite a lot of time
looking at the problem (we were not the only ones) and came up with
an enclosure. Unfortunately it would have cost about $2000, so we
learned to live with a slight shimmy on the display.

The problem is that for magnetic shielding you need an alloy known
as mu-metal, which is rather expensive and seldom used in large
enclosures. The earlier displays were lower resolution and had better
internal shielding (they also weighed a ton - well 80 pounds).

I think that LCDs are probably the answer, I don't know if 300 gauss
is enough to annoy a plasma display - you may want to test before
buying.

John Stott




