  the OpenVMS Programming Manual; using the OpenVMS support, one can easily
  implement centralized condition handlers and signals under OpenVMS, and
  one can also easily implement a condition handling model with more endemic
  one-per-operation handlers.)

  If using C, the basic test looks like this:

	#include <stsdef.h>
	RetStat = Mumble();
	if ( !$VMS_STATUS_SUCCESS( RetStat ))
	    return RetStat;

  If using VAX macro, the test looks like this:

	calls	#0,g^Mumble
	blbc	r0,error

  If the low bit is set, the operation succeeded.  There was a deliberate
  design choice made in OpenVMS to provide this -- the OpenVMS operating
  system provides multiple success codes, and multiple failure codes of
  various severities, and provides an easy way to perform a blanket "it
  worked" or "it failed" test. 

  I've worked with various applications written for other operating systems,
  and I've worked on other operating systems, and I've often found the error
  reporting in these situations to be rather inconsistent -- sometimes zero
  is success and non-zero is failure, sometimes it's reversed.  When zero
  is a failure code, one occasionally has to resort to dependence on a
  non-reentrant data cell (C routines use errno here) to determine the
  reason for the failure.  One then needs errno for each thread (or AST)
  of execution, where the OpenVMS model is rather easier to deal with.

  The OpenVMS scheme certainly appears more baroque when compared with
  other schemes and it can certainly be misused by folks testing for one
  particular explicit success (or failure) code, but the scheme is what
  makes generic recovery routines possible -- one does not need to code
  each possible status code, yet one can also easily choose to special-case
  a particular set of status codes, status codes from a particular facility,
  or status codes of a particular severity level.

  ------------------------------ Opinionative -------------------------------
   Stephen Hoffman      OpenVMS Engineering      hoffman@xdelta.enet.dec.com
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------




