|>Mike Zeleznik <zeleznik@venus.cs.utah.edu> wrote:
|>>OSF seems to limit memory allocation to 128MB per chunk.  Is there any way
|>>to increase this?  DEC Alpha, running OSF/3.2.
| ...
|>I did notice that I can't mlock() more than about 128MB (actually, slightly
|>higher, a little over 129MB), but that may be because of a limit on maximum
|>amount of locked memory - I get EWOULDBLOCK.
|>-- 
|>Steve Peltz
|>tricorn@uiuc.edu
