You've indeed with a tunable limit on how much physical memory can be
wired from programs. By default, no more that around 80% of your system's
phsyical memory can be wired. If you dare, you can go a little higher
by tweaking /etc/sysconfigtab:

vm:
	vm-syswiredpercent = 85

or something. I wouldn't recommend it, though. 
