I believe you're still slightly confused.  There is no such thing as an Alpha
Vax.  It's either an Alpha (aka AXP) or it's a Vax.  They are 2 different
architectures.

As the for the 2100, there are 2 different RISC systems.  One is based on the
MIPS CPU and ran Ultrix, and the other is based on the Alpha AXP CPU and runs
one of Digital Unix (formerly OSF/1), Windows/NT, or OpenVMS for Alpha.

Finally, to make matters even more confusing, OSF/1 has been renamed to Digital
Unix, just like VAX/VMS was renamed to OpenVMS for Vax.

