>
>[ customer is trying to boot a DECstation 5000/200 from a TK50 ]
>
>boot -f tz(0,5)

This isn't the boot command for the 5000 Model 200, though it might
be have been a very long time ago.  It is the syntax for the DECstation
3100.  The 5000/200 (and 100 and 240/260s) syntax is:

boot tc#/device/kernel

tc#    - TURBOchannel number (5 in this case)
device - Device name (tz5)
kernel - Not applicable to tape, usually vmunix or genvmunix for disk.

so:

boot 5/tz5

