I do have an AlphaStation 4 400/233 with both OSF/1 *AND* NT on two
separate disks. In the OSF/1 console modus, I type

	>>>set os_type nt

and power-cycle the machine, and it will restart with the ARC console
for booting NT. The ARC-console has a menu-entry for switching to OSF/1.

So, it's absolutely *NO* problem with DEC AlphaStations. As I
understand, for machines with the EISA-bus, You have to run the
EISA-config utility, but this should also be quite simple....

Lukas




