Vinay>  is around 1.5M.

According to the SOC, the AS 2100 doesn't support both internal and
external disks at the same time on one controller.  And the external
cabling can only be 1.0M if you do use external devices.  In general,
you should spend the money and get the disk carriers to put the disks
in the StorageWorks slots built into the system.  The part number for
the carrier is:

	SWXBA-Bx	3.5" carrier, x=A for fixed media,
				      x=B for removeable media.


