>Does anyone out there know the wiring of the original MicroVAX II
>console cable?  What I am after specifically is which pins are
>connected together on the 9-pin (CPU) end.  This is an undocumented
>feature of those cables.  Any help will be greatly appreciated
>including just the part number so I can try to dig up a cable on
>the used/surplus market.  Many thanks in advance.

>-- Aaron Sliwinski (aarons@ihs.com)

The 9pin you refer to is a standard 9 pin NULL modem RS-232 cable.

Route 1:
You call Datastorm (314-443-3282) and ask to purchase a Hotwire cable.
This wonderful NULL modem cable has both 9 and 25 pin
connectors on both ends, so there isn't much you can't hook up!  BTW
don't ask me how much it cost, I work here I got mine free. I personally
use one to talk to my uVAX II.

Route 2:
Run down to your local Radio Shack and buy a 9 pin to 25 pin Rs-232
cable and a 25 to 25 pin NULL modem converter or a 9 to 9 pin NULL
modem connector and be happy. (watch the gender!)

Route 3:
Else you can build your own...

	vax-9pin	terminal-25pin
	DCD 1		1  unused(FG)
	RD  2		2  TD
	TD  3		3  RD
	DTR 4		4  RTS
	SG  5		5  CTS
	DSR 6		6  DSR
	RTS 7		7  SG
	CTS 8		8  DCD
unused(RI)  9		20 DTR

1&6 --> 20
2   --> 2
3   --> 3
4   --> 6&8
5   --> 7
7   --> 5
8   --> 4

DCD -- Data Carrier Detect
RD  -- Receive Data
TD  -- Transmit Data
DTR -- Data Terminal Ready
SG  -- Signal Ground
DSR -- Data Set Ready
RTS -- Request to Send Signal
CTS -- Clear to Send Signal
RI  -- Ring Indicator  (unused)
FG  -- Floating Ground (unused)

Note: This is a NULL modem cable, so don't hook it up to a modem and
expect it to work.  These cables are designed for PC to PC (DTE to DTE)
xfers.

jam
