     The board comes in different flavors, but basically it is shipped
     as board only, with CPU (no cache, no DRAM).  It can be
     configured with different sets of firmware (NT or Digital UNIX),
     and comes with either AT or PS2 keyboard.

>   What documentation (part numbers?) is available for this board?

     There is a design guide available at:

        ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/axppci                (U.S.)
        ftp://ftp.digital.de/pub/Digital/oem/boards/AXPpci33    (Europe)

>   What disk and video controllers are supported?

     Which OS?  For Windows NT you should see the Hardware
     Compatibility List from Microsoft.

     The SCSI controller is on board (PCI/SCSI NCR53C810).

>   Does anyone in the Southern California area have one that
>   I can take a look at?

     Not really close, but you can see a picture at:

        http://www.digital.de/oem/products/boards/AXPpci33.html

