Two interesting questions have been raised in this thread:

1. "Would anybody mind if I were to mirror it..."

	In most cases, we'd be grateful to have someone mirror the site.
	However, with FreePort Express, we're
 
	o Beta testing the software at present -- we'd like to avoid uncontrolled
	  proliferation of this relatively early version of the software

	o Testing the distribution channel

	To the extent possible, we'd like to restrict distribution to the
	NovaLink site so that we can track the number of copies that are
	down-loaded, see where they go, etc. Also, as I recall, the on-line
	license requests that you get the software directly from our
        distribution point. I'm afraid that the lawyers insisted :-}

2. Why did we park at NovaLink instead of .digital.com?

	Again, we're experimenting and testing, though I hope that we will soon
	have at least a cross reference from .digital.com to the NovaLink site.

Over time, as we get smarter, we'll get better.

Thanks for your interest!
/andy

