Subject: Need Help/Info on VAX-BI Bus Problem
Date: 1995/08/10
Message-ID: <40diu0$5n3@theopolis.orl.mmc.com>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 107906675
distribution: world
organization: Martin Marietta - Information Systems
reply-to: schwarz@sunny.dab.ge.com
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec,comp.os.vms,vmsnet.admin,vmsnet.internals

Hello,

  We have a VAX 7000-620 with a VAX-BI bucket with every slot full. We are running
VMS 6.0. One of these boards is and HSD/DRB32-M combo that is occasionally hanging
up.  I have traced the problem to a timeout of the FIFO read between ths HSD board
and the DRB32-M.  We have found that by reducing the number of buffered I/O's the 
problem goes away. Reducing the number of direct I/O's reduced the occurance of the
problem, but not completly. 

Our run which was causing the problem had 840 DIO's + 528 BIO's = 1368 i/o's per sec.
Reducing the DIO's to 600 + 528 BIO's = 1128 i/o/s reduced the problem. Reducing
the BIO to 288 + 840 DIO's = 1128 i/o/s seemed to eliminate the problem.

I have assumed that we are overloading the VAX-BI backplane which is preventing 
the HSD driver from communicating commands to the board. Although the reduction in
I/O seems to fix the problem, I am nervous about claiming the problem is 100% fixed.
Mainly because I am not certain of my assumtion as to what is happing. This is due
to fact that I have two of these HSD/DRB32 cards that fail, but I also have other
DRB32 boards and DMB32 boards that are not exhibiting any problems. Also the 
aggregate througput is ~440 Kb/s, which I assume is well below the capability of the
system. 

So, could anyone give me any aggreement or disagreement with my analysis?

Could someone provide capacity data on bandwidth and maximum number of I/O's for the
BI's? 

Any kind of help would be appreciated. I have tried the Digital www pages and
bookreader to no avail.

Thanks,

Jim


