In article <3vr5ka$acn@news.hic.net>, bdwebb@hic.net (Brian D. Webb) writes:
> I'm trying to learn how to protect VMS software from running on 
> unauthorized machines.  I'm currently trying to get a serial port 
> hardware key to work, but would like to know what other methods or 
> products are available.  Please e-mail me if you can help.

If this is for software to be used only within your own company, you
could check the Ethernet address.

If this is for software you intend to sell to others, license PAKGEN
from DEC or rely exclusively on legal agreements.  Checking machine
characteristics does _not_ fly in the VMS commercial world.  If you
don't believe me, try asking the same question on comp.os.vms.

Larry Kilgallen



