In article <3vodif$44ch@yuma.ACNS.ColoState.EDU>, murph@holly.ColoState.EDU (John Murphy) writes:
>
>I have a decstation 5000/200 that has a S> boot prompt.  I need to get it
>to the regular >> boot prompt, so I can boot it to single user mode.  Does
>anybody know what this mode is, and how to get out of it?

This is the secure console mode.  I think the only commands supported
are "boot" and "password".  To get it out this mode use the password
command to give it the password.

Don't know the password?  Shut the system down and open the box.  On
the CPU module, just in front of the TURBOchannel slot nearest the
power supply are two blocks of jumpers; a set of four, probsably on
a red mount and a pair two.  This is also near where the board ways
"WSE".  Turn the power off, short the pair, turn the power on and
after a couple of seconds turn the power off.  This will clear the
CPU's NVRAM where the password is stored.  It will also clear the
boot path and boot mode.

