From the standard

"It is unspecified whether errno is a macro or an identifier declared with
external linkage. If a macro definition is suppressed in order to access an
actual object, or the program defines an identifier with the name errno,
the behaviour is undefined".

Given that and the fact that a structure member name is an identifier
Dec 'C's implementation is correct and the fault is with the code.

