Rob Radvanovsky <helix@solaria.sol.net> wrote:
>Have a possibility to get an old VAX-11/750 with all the trimmings. 
>Figure that it will have (at least 512 KB of onboard memory and hopefully
>200 MB of disk space).  I'm looking for an old copy of the BSD-style of
>UNIX (v3.1, 3.2 or 3.3) that will work (specifically) for the VAX-11/730,
>11/750 or 11/780 models of the VAX-11 series computers.
>
>Any ideas on this one, folks?

I don't know what's involved in getting an old copy of BSD (a
license from AT&T for one thing, most likely).  But there's a
NetBSD port to the VAX in progress.  NetBSD derives from 4.4 BSD
Lite.  And you're in luck--so far NetBSD runs on only two VAX
models, and the 11/750 is one of them.  (MicroVAX II's are the
other kind.)  However, it looks to me like you'll need at least
2MB of memory, and NetBSD only supports certain drive
controllers, etc. at this point.  And I gather that this is
alpha-test level software.  See http://www.netbsd.org or
ftp.netbsd.org for more information.

