newsgroups: comp.os.vms,comp.sys.dec

We have been having some problems with our modem setup, and I was
wondering if anyone had seen similar problems before.

Hardware:
Alpha Server 1000 4/200 running OpenVMS V6.1-1H2
DECserver 90L+ V2.0 BL5.5 Protocol: LAT V5.2
DECserver 200 V3.3 BL39 Protocol: LAT V5.1

We have three modems connected to the DECserver, and our terminals are
connected to the 90L+.  We use KERMIT to dial out.

Sometimes, a process running KERMIT (C-Kermit 5A(189), 30 June 93,
OpenVMS AXP) will get into an unrecoverable state where all keyboard
input is stopped (the terminal's output buffer will fill up if you
continually press keys). This always happens when KERMIT is
"connected" to the port (i.e., keystrokes are being passed to the
modem).

The usual solution is for the user to hit BREAK, return back to the
90L prompt, and disconnect the session.  This all works properly, but
when they try to reconnect to the Alpha, they get the error,
"%90L-311, Illegal message" and get immediately disconnected.
Furthermore, everybody who has an active session on the 90L gets
disconnected with the same error message and when background sessions
are resumed, they die immediately as well.  Basically, when the
culprit tries to reconnect, EVERY SESSION that was active at that
point in time on the server gets "tainted", and dies when it is
activated.

We have called Digital, but they are scratching their heads, and seem
to be reluctant to help out because the only time we experience this
problem is when we use KERMIT.  Has anyone else seen this problem, or
does anyone know any hints?  We have had networking problems with this
Alpha since day one, when "mcr ncp show known nodes" would crash the
system. :) But, this is the first time we've set up terminals and
modems on servers (we had an MVII before with 16 serial ports), so I'm
not ruling anything out.

Thanks in advance,

Marc. (mrami@minerva.cis.yale.edu)



