X-Deja-AN: 107424131
references: <3vr999$2s3@explorer.csc.com>
organization: Flying Disk Systems, Inc.
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec

In article <3vr999$2s3@explorer.csc.com>, 
rmsmith@csc.com (Robert Smith) writes:

> The uVII has 5 LEDs on it - 4 red, 1 green.
> What does the green one mean? what do the reds ones mean?

Green = DC power OK.
The red ones map to the four bits of a single hex digit,
displayed on the back panel.

> I picked up another uVII.  It hangs with an F on the console display
> LED, four red LEDs on on the cpu board, and never goes any further in
> self diag.
> I am going thru my docs but do not find ref to these LEDs...

They are described in the KA630-AA CPU Module User's Guide,
order number EK-KA630-UG.   The sequence goes something
like this:

F = DC power has been applied.
E = The first instruction in the boot ROM has been executed.
    (It writes the proper value to the display register.)
D = The power-up stabilization wait and the power-up mode
    detection routine has completed.
C = The ROM checksum had been validated.

etc.

