thomasgd@boat.bt.com (Greg Thomas) writes: I'm trying to porting some
>code to Alpha/DEC 'C' from VAX/VAX 'C'. We have, however, hit a
>problem with the <errno.h> include file. It #defines it to be
>(*cma$tis_errno_get_addr()). The trouble is, we have number of
>structures that have an errno as an element. Of course, this gets
>expanded to the above function, and so it won't compile. ie ...

The problem is because ISO does not allow "$" in identifiers, but _some_
compilers do in order to access system-defined identifiers with "$" in
them---VAX VMS is notably one that has a few (do I remember SMG$ cor-
rectly?). Just a guess, but are you including the correct headers for
your _current_ compiler?

Best regards,
Derick.
