In article <3vr999$2s3@explorer.csc.com>, rmsmith@csc.com (Robert Smith) writes:
:The uVII has 5 LEDs on it - 4 red, 1 green.
:What does the green one mean? what do the reds ones mean?
:
:I picked up another uVII.  It hangs with an F on the console display
:LED, four red leds on on the cpu board, and never goes any further in
:self diag.
:
:I am going thru my docs but do not find ref to these leds...
:thanks in advance for any help!

  These LEDs are likely covered in the KA630 CPU technical user's guide
  (the part is EK-KA630-UG), and the "stuck-on-F" indicator means that the
  module self-test has detected a hard fault -- the four red illuminated
  LEDs mirrors the hex F, as well.

  I don't have the guide handy to tell you exactly what failed the test,
  but "F" means that a very low-level test failed.

