>Does anyone know how I can reliably detect the presence of the following from
>C (Borland or MSVC), from within Windows 3.x, WfW, NT, Win95...?
>   - LAT services
>   - Pathworks 4.X
>   - Pathworks 5.X
>

For LAT, check the DOS environment variable NVTWIN. Should be 1 if LAT is used 
with Windows.

For Pathworks 4.X, check _SYSD. Should be equal to system service drive letter 
if network is running.
Could probably get network entries from the system.ini file using 
GetPrivateProfileString.
Maybe there's even a DLL call to check the name of the running network.

For Pathworks 5.X - sorry, no ideas. Still on 4.2-1.

