In article <evm.807227172@pacifier> evm@pacifier.com (Ethan VanMatre) writes:


Ethan> I'm looking to see if anyone has added 3 turbo channel scsi
Ethan> adapters to a decstation 5000/240. With the built in scsi that
Ethan> would make 4 scsi bus. I should call this system a Dec system
Ethan> as that there would be no graphics controller installed (only 3
Ethan> turbo slots).

We've got a total of two SCSI controllers on our 5000/260 and it works
well.  I seem to remember that DEC has a dual SCSI controller single
TC board controller as well, but I can find it in the systems and
options catalog.  

Another option is to get the TURBOchannel extender if you need more
controllers.   It's part number is PMTCE-AA

Ethan> I have a customer who wants to put 21 rz28 on a 240. Has it
Ethan> been done?  should work but has it?

I don't see why it shouldn't work.  Just get the SW300 RAID office
expansion which holds 24 devices without a problem.

If you use an HSZ40 RAID controller, you won't have a problem.  It
supports upto 42 SCSI-2 disks or solid state disks.  RAID 0 (striping)
is standard.  You theoretically could hang 7 of these of each
controller, but bandwidth and support issues intrude.

You might want to look into the KZTSA controller with an HSZ40 to
provide maximum bandwidth.

