In article <evm.807227172@pacifier>, evm@pacifier.com (Ethan VanMatre) writes:

>I'm looking to see if anyone has added 3 turbo channel scsi adapters to a 
>decstation 5000/240. With the built in scsi that would make 4 scsi bus. I 
>should call this system a Dec system as that there would be no graphics 
>controller installed (only 3 turbo slots).

I've never tried it myself, but it IS a supported configuration.  The
GENERIC configuration file knows to look for up to four SCSI adapters
and the V4.4 SPD very clearly indicates that 3 PMAZs are supported.  It
also indicates that a maximum of 28 disks are supported and the RZ28
is included.

It does suggest that the controller ID be set to be the highest ID on
the bus, so you may have to change the PMAZs, which may be factor set
at 6 instead of 7.
