PAUL D. CHAPIN (pdchapin@unix.amherst.edu) wrote:
: I've just added a new RZ drive to a Dec3000/600 running dUnix 3.2.
: When you load it up you get some default partition sizes, such as
: 131072 for a and so forth.  Does anybody know what this value is based
: on.  This doesn't appear to be an even number of cylinders or tracks.
: Could this have easily been 131070?

: --
: Paul Chapin

It either comes from the partition table written to the drive at
some time in its life, or it comes from the controller defaults.

You can inspect/change the partition table with the 'chpt' command
on Ultrix (you must be root).

Another source of information for disk partition parameters is
the /etc/disktab file which is consulted by the 'newfs' command.

Barry Kort



